y (conscientious), stress resilience, technical (weather assessment, computer). Weaknesses: memory for numbers (attention), nasty remarks (crew cooperation, communication).\n\nC: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership, regarded as show-off, not open to new ideas.\n\nStrengths: anticipation (decision quality, safety), complex connections (technical), spatial vision (technical), leadership (crew cooperation). Weaknesses: show-off (crew cooperation), not open to new ideas (adaptability).\n\nD: responds adequately to unexpected events, concentrates very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as know-it-all, hot temper.\n\nStrengths: adaptability to unexpected, concentration (attention), problem solving (technical), responsibility. Weaknesses: know-it-all (crew cooperation), hot temper (stress resilience, crew cooperation).\n\nWe need to start discussion. Perhaps pick candidate C as leading due to anticipation and leadership, but note concerns about openness. Or candidate B with reliability but nasty remarks. Or D with responsibility but hot temper. A has good decision and calm but communication issues.\n\nWe need to start with a recommendation and argue. Could choose Candidate C as leading, but note concerns. Provide evidence: anticipates dangerous situations, leadership, but show-off and not open to new ideas. That may be balanced.\n\nAlternatively, candidate B has conscientiousness and stress handling, but nasty remarks. That is serious for crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate D has responsibility and concentration, but hot temper.\n\nCandidate A has quick decisions and calm, but egocentric and poor communication.\n\nWhich is strongest overall? Probably C: strong technical, decision, leadership, but concerns about cooperation and adaptability. B also strong reliability but interpersonal issues. D also strong responsibility but hot temper.\n\nI think C may be best overall if we can mitigate show-off and openness concerns. So I will recommend Candidate C, but note concerns.\n\nThus public message: I propose Candidate C as current recommendation, referencing anticipation and leadership, but note concerns about being a show-off and not open to new ideas, which may affect crew cooperation and adaptability. Suggest we need to compare with others.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON vote: Candidate C."}
